        "ja-Hrkt": "ヤドン",
        "zh-Hans": "呆呆兽",
        "zh-Hant": "呆呆獸"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Slowpoke is famously slow on the uptake: it can take five seconds to feel pain and a whole day to notice something biting its tail. It fishes by dangling its sweet-tasting tail in the water, and if the tail breaks off, it just grows back. In some places its yawn is believed to bring rain, and Slowpoke is worshipped there.",
        "guide": "A pink, hippo-like Water and Psychic Pokémon known for being extremely slow to react. It fishes with its long, sweet-tasting tail, which grows back if it breaks off. It evolves into Slowbro or Slowking, and its Galarian form is a Psychic type.",
        "tagline": "Takes a whole day to notice its tail's been bitten",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Slowpoke (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Slowpoke_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "branches": {
        "text": "Slowpoke can go two ways: it evolves into Slowbro from level 37, or into Slowking, added in Generation 2, when traded holding a King's Rock. Galarian Slowpoke branches too, becoming Galarian Slowbro with a Galarica Cuff or Galarian Slowking with a Galarica Wreath, which makes Slowpoke the only Pokémon whose regional form has a branched evolution.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Slowpoke (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Slowpoke_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
