        "it": "Slowbro",
        "ja": "ヤドラン",
        "ko": "야도란",
        "ja-Hrkt": "ヤドラン",
        "zh-Hans": "呆壳兽",
        "zh-Hant": "呆殼獸"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "According to the Pokédex, a Shellder clamping onto Slowpoke's tail is what turns it into Slowbro. The Shellder's poison means Slowbro no longer feels pain, and since it can't fish with its tail any more, it swims after prey and lets the Shellder eat the scraps. If the Shellder falls off, Slowbro turns back into a Slowpoke.",
        "guide": "One of Slowpoke's two final forms, evolving from level 37. It is a bipedal Water and Psychic Pokémon with a Shellder biting its tail, and it is said to turn back into Slowpoke if the Shellder comes off. It can Mega Evolve into Mega Slowbro, and its Galarian form is a Poison and Psychic type.",
        "tagline": "Slowpoke plus a Shellder that won't let go",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Slowbro (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Slowbro_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
